# Google Search Console ownership tokens must survive git byte-exact.
#
# This machine has autocrlf on — every checkout of a text file rewrites its
# line endings. Today that happens to be harmless for the token, because the
# file is a single line with no newline in it at all and so has no LF to
# convert. That is luck, not a guarantee: a token issued with a trailing
# newline would be silently rewritten to CRLF on checkout, the body would no
# longer match what Google expects, and the property would quietly
# un-verify with nothing in the diff to show for it.
#
# -text switches the conversion off. -diff stops git trying to render a
# meaningless one-line diff of an opaque token.
#
# See the "Never delete" section in README.md.
public/google*.html -text -diff
